+# Energy opportunities for the live ARC agent — 2026-09-05
+
+Read-only review under the 2026-09-05 brief: "where, if anywhere, could a Carnot
+energy-based approach give the LIVE ARC agent more speed, accuracy, or efficiency?"
+The brief asked for the counter-question too: where would an energy proposal be
+novelty-seeking dressed as research? This note answers both. No code was changed.
+`results/**` was read and never written.
+
+## 0. Verdict, stated first
+
+**There is no genuine new energy opportunity on the live path. The bottleneck is
+elsewhere.** Three facts carry the verdict; each is measured below with its population.
+
+1. **Energy is already on the live path, and it measured neutral or null in every
+   slot.** Engine selection (`trust_energy`, S2-v3), plan guidance (`goal_energy`, S3),
+   candidate generation (energy-fitness QD), action pruning (three pruner prototypes and
+   the value head), and win-state recognition (state-goal energy) were each built, wired,
+   and measured. None banked a level the bare explorer did not.
+2. **The two measured bottlenecks are not scoring problems.** Wall clock is 98 percent
+   generator decode that emits lookup tables. Action count is first-contact discovery by
+   a blind explorer that finds the win by stumbling into it. An energy function ranks
+   candidates; it cannot shorten a decode or invent a hypothesis the inducer never wrote.
+3. **The score arithmetic closes the efficiency door for partial gains.** RHAE squares
+   the human-to-agent action ratio. On r11l level 0 the agent used 815 actions against a
+   human 22. Halving the agent's actions moves the level score from 0.07 to 0.29 points
+   out of 100. Only near-human action counts score, and those need a correct model of
+   the game, which is the generation wall again.
+
+"Nowhere new" is the honest answer. Section 4 lists every candidate considered and the
+measurement that rejects it, so the next session does not re-derive them. Section 5
+records two hygiene items that convert the standing prose ban into checks.
+
+## 1. Scope and what "energy" means here
+
+Scope is the LIVE agent per CLAUDE.md "ARC Live-Path Reachability Discipline":
+`python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py` (`E3AgentPolicy`, `make_carnot_agent`,
+the scored path) and `scripts/arc_loop_solve.py` (the offline twin).
+
+In this note "energy" means a scalar score, learned or hand-built, that ranks states,
+transitions, engines, or actions. That is Carnot's verifier-as-scorer. It excludes the
+deterministic execution check that defines correctness: running an induced engine on
+recorded transitions and comparing grids. Per the Circularity / Oracle-Distinctness
+Discipline, that check is the oracle. An energy that only re-runs it is
+`execution_grounded`, not a moat.
+
+Sources read: CLAUDE.md in full; the memory files named in the brief plus the ARC-specific
+ones; `ops/known-issues.md` 2026-06-26 (the S0 conclusion);
+`docs/research-notes/oracle-distinct-structural-energy-program-2026-06-26.md`;
+`docs/research-notes/arc-agi3-levers-tried-x-verdict-2026-06-25.md` (the levers ledger);
+`docs/research-notes/arc-live-agent-baseline-four-axes-2026-09-04.md`;
+`docs/research-notes/post-nctx-induce-engines-are-lookup-tables-2026-09-04.md`;
+`ops/verifier_gaps.md` GAP-ARCH-WORLD-MODEL-TRUST-ENERGY, GAP-ARCH-FRAME-CHANGE-PREDICTOR,
+GAP-WM-TRUST-GATE; `ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml`; the eval artifacts under
+`results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/`; and the agent source at the lines cited.
+Artifacts were read through `scripts/summarize_artifact.py` where the reader applies.
+
+## 2. Bottleneck map
+
+Every number names its population. "One run" means exactly that.
+
+### 2.1 Wall clock: the generator, and the generator alone
+
+| quantity | value | population |
+|---|---|---|
+| classical path, LLM off | 272 actions in about 1 s, about 4 ms per action | one r11l run, budget 300, `CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_INDUCTION=1` (baseline note, 2026-09-04) |
+| whole game, LLM on | about 24,998 s for 2,077 actions | `results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/r11l-2491317.json`; seconds inferred from run log and file times, the artifact has no duration field |
+| generator share | about 98 percent by subtraction | the two rows above |
+| generator output | 13 chat completions; 2,467,130 reasoning chars; 37,872 final chars (98.5 percent reasoning) | same artifact, `generator_channels` |
