+
+The offline structural energy itself is real: S0' LOO AUROC 0.739 leak-clean, S1 0.713
+over 10 seeds with a descent direction. It is an offline cross-game discriminator that
+adds nothing to the live agent. That is the program's own conclusion (`ops/known-issues.md`
+2026-06-26), and CLAUDE.md forbids re-proposing its stages.
+
+## 4. Candidates considered
+
+Each candidate was judged on the brief's five questions: measured bottleneck and
+population; what energy adds over the current mechanism; oracle-distinct or circular;
+headroom; cheap falsifier. The rejections come first because they are most of the value.
+
+### 4.1 REJECTED
+
+**R1. Energy to select among induced engines.** Bottleneck: not selection. Comparator:
+the execution-grounded accuracy gate, which is free. S2-v3 measured neutral corpus-wide
+(23 of 25 games effective, positive control passed). Raising Kaggle concurrency to K=16
+gives about 13 inductions per game, so selection matters more there; S2-v3 already used
+enforced diverse pools, so the verdict carries. Forbidden as a re-proposal by CLAUDE.md.
+
+**R2. Energy to guide `plan_in_model` toward the goal.** S3 measured zero new winners on
+24 headroom games with guidance verified to have changed proposals. exp4640 and exp4737
+measured the goal-energy variant at zero lift and 0 of 100. The goal predicate never
+fires (2.3), so any goal energy compiled from it is constant. Forbidden as a re-proposal.
+
+**R3. Energy-as-fitness generation (quality-diversity, MAP-Elites).** exp4653 null; the
+first-contact exploration-signal family is retired on the exclusion manifest with
+`energy-as-fitness first-contact rerun` as a blocked pattern. Needs an operator override
+citing a new mechanism, and none is on offer here.
+
+**R4. Verifier-as-action-pruner or learned value head for efficiency.** The most
+tempting slot, because efficiency is the scored axis, and the most thoroughly swept.
+Hard-argmax pruner: median efficiency ratio 1.042 and lost m0r0 (`proto_carnot_pruner`).
+Hedged and abstaining variants: no deployable arm. Live value routing (exp4652/4658/4665):
+first-win 0.04 both arms, delta 0.0, CI [0,0]; `value_weight` reverted 5 to 0 because the
+live search got slower and solved fewer games. Offline-replay pruners (exp3929 1.96x,
+exp4160 1.31x, exp4071 67 percent) never pruned a winning action on already-solved traces
+and banked no level; exp4071 ran on 3 games with replay wall clock minus 199 percent.
+Section 2.4 shows why even a real 50 percent cut cannot move the score. Cross-game value
+transfer is retired (`cross_game_value_transfer_retired_exp4342_v401`).
+
+**R5. Retrain the frame-change CNN as an affordance energy.** Four adversarially verified
+nulls in one session (REQ-ARC-FCP-5590/5728/5729/5730). The headline 0.709 did not
+reproduce (0.539 over 5 seeds) and an action-id-only base rate scored higher (0.549). The
+gap entry forbids a retrain of the same frame-only architecture. See 4.3 for the one
+open door this leaves, and why it is still not proposed.
+
+**R6. State or goal energy to recognise win states.** `arc3_state_goal_energy_discrimination`:
+mean leave-one-game-out AUROC 0.4958 against a shuffled control of 0.509. Chance. An
+energy that cannot tell a win state from a non-win state cannot guide toward one.
+
+**R7. Transition-EBM reranker.** GAP-3 stage 2 and 2v2: macro AUROC 0.5442, hit set a
+strict subset of vote's, retired on the manifest
+(`gap3_trained_content_energy_selector_retired_stage2v2_2026_06_09`). Reopen needs
+operator authorisation plus the gate-1R redesign.
+
+**R8. Energy-as-RFT-teacher for the generator.** Levers ledger "DO NOT RE-OPEN": the
+cross-game certifier is at chance (R7), and the winner is never proposed (R2), so the
+certified-correct training set is empty. The one positive (Sudoku +1.1 percent) used the
+true oracle, not a learned energy. Also blocked by the live-agent framing: the scored
+path runs frozen weights offline.
+
+**R9. Energy over the reasoning stream to stop a bad induce early.** This is the only
+candidate aimed at the 98 percent wall-clock bottleneck, so it deserves a full answer.
+What it would need: a scorer on partial reasoning text that predicts a lookup-table
+engine before decode finishes. What exists: the verifier ensemble is math-bound (FoVer
+0.9131, PRMBench 0.552, facts earned-negative, code weak); the Phase D external-text
+scorer line (LoRA-EBM, uPRM, EBRM) is retired after seven milestones
+(`phase_d_external_text_scorer_retired_exp5163_v474`); the live ARC LLM corpus is about
+47 rows total, so there is nothing to train a new one on. FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK applies in
+reverse: no positive control could even be run. The honest comparators are non-energy:
+`CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_THINKING_BUDGET` (an accuracy A/B; think-off measured worse, held-out
+0.100 vs 0.373 in exp6199) and Kaggle concurrency (per-stream throughput is fixed at
+about 31 tok/s; only aggregate changes). Rejected.
+
+**R10. Energy as a lookup-table or memorisation detector.** The held-out split
+(`_split_prefix_heldout`, last third of rows) already detects it exactly: 100 percent
+prefix, 50 to 75 percent held out, in 5 of 6 near-miss cells. `arc_engine_static_validation.py`
+already catches broken code before the gate. Both are deterministic and cost milliseconds
+against a 25-minute decode. An energy here would re-run the oracle: circular by
+definition. The fix is on the generation side (prompt, format, or model), not scoring.
+
+**R11. Hardware-accelerated energy evaluation.** The classical path costs 4 ms per
+action end to end. There is nothing to accelerate. Paper-v6 narrowing also forbids any
+KV260-speedup framing at current dimensions.
+
+**R12. Energy as an intrinsic curiosity or progress bonus.** `arc_dense_curiosity_progress`
+is live-reachable and was disabled in the measured run. The exploration-signal family is
+retired (R3). The 2026-06-29 structural finding stands: the winning prefix on the wall
+games is not a function of observable state (exp4914 `WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE`), so an
+observable-state bonus cannot point at it.
+
+**R13. The hidden-state "moat slot" (GAP-ARCH-WORLD-MODEL-TRUST-ENERGY, status open).**
+The gap entry predates the program that answered it. S2-v3 covered 23 of 25 games,
+including the hidden-state set, and measured neutral. The entry's status is stale; see 5.
+
+**R14. Any restaging of S0 to S4.** CLAUDE.md: "do NOT re-propose S4/ARC-energy stages".
+Not a judgement call.
+
+### 4.2 PROPOSED
+
+None that build energy.
+
+The brief allowed this answer and asked that no proposal be manufactured. Every slot
+where an energy could sit on the live path has an energy in it or a measured null
+against it, and the two bottlenecks that remain (decode wall clock, first-contact
+discovery) are not ranking problems. A ranked list with one manufactured entry would be
+the novelty-seeking the brief warned against.
+
+### 4.3 The one open door, and why it is still not proposed
+
+GAP-ARCH-FRAME-CHANGE-PREDICTOR's revised candidate design (b) names a contrastive,
+pairwise objective that must discriminate WITHIN an action id, not across ids. A
+contrastive scorer is energy-shaped, so an adversarial reader will ask why it is not in
+4.2. Four reasons, in order of weight.
+
+1. **Expected value is bounded by 2.4.** Even a scorer that halves level-0 actions moves
+   r11l from 0.07 to 0.29 points. The action-effect prior already scores every frontier
+   candidate (2.2) and the agent still needs 815 actions, so the marginal cut would be
+   smaller than half.
+2. **The honest comparator is free and already live.** The action-id base rate, which
+   `PersistentAEM` carries, scored 0.549 held-out against the CNN's 0.539. Any new scorer
+   must beat it by a margin with a CI that excludes zero, before any live A/B.
+3. **It is a representation problem, not an energy problem.** The record's own diagnosis
+   is that both tested representations reduce to a per-action-type base rate. The
+   missing piece is an action-by-frame-location interaction feature. Calling that
+   "Carnot energy" would be the origin-story reflex.
+4. **Four nulls stand against the closest design.** Rerun discipline requires a named
+   difference, and the difference here is a loss function on the same inputs.
+
+If someone insists on testing it, the cheap falsifier is offline and CPU-only: on the
+existing banked transitions, within-action-id AUROC for "this action changes the frame"
+minus the action-id-only baseline, leave-one-game-out, 5 seeds, CI95 excluding zero at
++0.05 or better; then an actions-to-first-level A/B on the explorer-only sweep set with
+`run_seeded_progress` (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5720). Cost: hours. Prior: low. Not recommended.
+
